       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The total daily dose looks like an error.\n\n- **Ordered:** metformin 1700 mg \u00d7 3 per day = **5,100 mg/day**.\n- **Maximum labeled dose:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release in many labels.\n- **Risk:** The order is about twice the maximum. That raises the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nPossible intended orders:\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- 500 mg PO three times daily with meals (1,500 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg total per day, split into divided doses (for example, 850 mg twice daily)\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you do want 1700 mg three times daily, confirm that and I'll enter it with a note saying the dose was intentionally confirmed. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
